        "id": 9252,
        "name": "SuperRick",
        "username": "SuperRick",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/superrick/{size}/2705_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-11T23:04:26.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Okay!&nbsp; Just played my fourth games and my daughter and I had a great time!&nbsp; I played Scholar and she played Fanatic (with a support deck, H=3)&nbsp;and we took on Ambuscade on Insula Primis, and it was definitly memorable!&nbsp; I can't remember the exact play-by-play, but it went something like this:</p><p>1. The game started out with us getting our butts kicked by the devices that Ambuscade started with.&nbsp; Then he&nbsp;kept putting more of them out there and it was NOT looking good.&nbsp; I was thinking to myself,&nbsp;<em>Crap,&nbsp;maybe I should be playing a third hero here...</em></p><p>2. My daughter figgured out that the immedite threat&nbsp;was not Ambuscade's shield but rather his devices that were attacking us (she's only 7, but I let her&nbsp;figure a lot of stuff on her own&nbsp;and she enjoys it more that way).&nbsp; So she (Fanatic) started attacking the devices and not the shields.&nbsp; Oh, and she pulled her relic sword out and the environment was buffing everyone's damage.</p><p>3. I (Scholar) started to get something going as well.&nbsp; The damage that Ambuscade was dealing kept going to the highest hit point hero, which was me at that time (we were going back and forth on HP until I just happened to have more).&nbsp; Well, I started putting down cards that made it to where I absorbed zero damage.&nbsp; We felt like we were starting to get the situation under control.</p><p>4. My little girl pulls out&nbsp;End of Days and Ambuscade said, \"Oh&nbsp;snap.\"&nbsp; The board was wiped clean: no shields, no devices, nothing for anyone.&nbsp; It hurt Ambuscade a lot more than it hurt us.&nbsp;</p><p>5. Ambuscade couldn't really recover and Fanatic was down to 15 points when she pulled Wrathful Retribution (I think that's the name of it).&nbsp; It took him down 15 hit points, the difference between her current HP and her max HP.&nbsp; Anyways, at that point we pretty much had him beat.</p><p>6. We won!&nbsp;</p><p>It was great because we thought we were toast and then it all came together.&nbsp;</p>",
